---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About · Online Chalisa"
  description="Why Online Chalisa exists — a distraction-free, ad-free, privacy-respecting home for sacred Hindu hymns."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main" class="pb-24">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 pt-16 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-(--mute)">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-(--ink) sm:text-5xl">
        A sanctuary, not a website.
      </h1>

      <div class="reader mt-8 space-y-6 text-(--body)">
        <p>
          Online Chalisa was built for one reason: the sacred texts most people love — Hanuman
          Chalisa, Shiv Chalisa, Ganesh, Durga, Shani — are trapped on the modern web behind
          banner ads, autoplay video, popup subscriptions, and menus for cricket scores.
        </p>
        <p>
          None of that belongs anywhere near a hymn.
        </p>
        <p>
          So we built the opposite. A quiet page. Warm typography. A sepia mode for warm morning
          reading and a true dark mode for night. A single button to hide every scrap of interface.
          A hands-free teleprompter for older devotees who prefer to read seated with folded hands.
          Optional audio at the bottom, ready to fade away when you enter <em>Zen mode</em>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-(--ink)">What we don't do</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li class="list-disc">No advertisements, ever.</li>
          <li class="list-disc">No third-party trackers or analytics of your reading.</li>
          <li class="list-disc">No account, sign-up, or email required.</li>
          <li class="list-disc">No push notifications or nagging reminders.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="pt-4 font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-(--ink)">Sankalp is yours</h2>
        <p>
          The streak tracker lives entirely in your browser's local storage. It never leaves your
          device. If you clear browser data, it will reset — that is the price of privacy, and
          we think it's a fair one.
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-4 font-serif text-2xl font-medium text-(--ink)">On the text</h2>
        <p>
          The Devanagari verses and Roman transliterations are drawn from long-standing devotional
          traditions and cross-referenced against multiple published editions. If you spot an
          error, please let us know — accuracy in scripture is a matter of care.
        </p>

        <p class="pt-4 text-center font-serif text-lg text-(--ink)">
          ॥ शुभम् अस्तु ॥
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
